## The guard component

```jsx
function RequireAuth({ children }) {
  const { user, isLoading } = useAuth();
  const location = useLocation();

  if (isLoading) return <Spinner />;   // do not redirect before you know

  if (!user) {
    // Remember the destination so login can send them back
    return <Navigate to="/login" state={{ from: location }} replace />;
  }

  return children;
}

<Route path="/dashboard" element={
  <RequireAuth><Dashboard /></RequireAuth>
} />
```

The `isLoading` check matters: without it, a page refresh briefly has no user and bounces an authenticated person to the login screen.

`replace` matters too — otherwise the protected URL stays in history and the back button loops.

