## Server-rendered apps

With Next.js, do the check in middleware or a Server Component so the protected content never reaches the browser at all — a strictly better position than rendering and then hiding.

## Schema-driven validation

```jsx
import { z } from 'zod';
import { useForm } from 'react-hook-form';
import { zodResolver } from '@hookform/resolvers/zod';

const schema = z.object({
  email: z.string().email('Enter a valid email address'),
  password: z.string().min(8, 'Password must be at least 8 characters'),
  confirm: z.string(),
}).refine((d) => d.password === d.confirm, {
  message: 'Passwords do not match',
  path: ['confirm'],
});

type FormValues = z.infer<typeof schema>;   // the type comes free
```

One schema gives you client validation, the TypeScript type, and — if you share it — server validation.

