## Accessible markup

```jsx
function EmailField({ register, error }) {
  const id = useId();
  const errorId = `${id}-error`;

  return (
    <div>
      <label htmlFor={id}>Email</label>
      <input
        id={id}
        type="email"
        aria-invalid={error ? 'true' : undefined}
        aria-describedby={error ? errorId : undefined}
        {...register('email')}
      />
      {error && (
        <p id={errorId} role="alert" className="text-red-700">
          {error.message}
        </p>
      )}
    </div>
  );
}
```

Four details doing the work:

1. `htmlFor` / `id` — clicking the label focuses the input, and screen readers announce the field name
2. `aria-invalid` — the field is announced as invalid
3. `aria-describedby` — the error is read out as part of the field
4. `role="alert"` — the message is announced when it appears, without moving focus

