## On submit failure, move focus

```jsx
// Send focus to the first invalid field so keyboard and screen reader
// users are not left at the bottom of the form wondering what happened
useEffect(() => {
  const first = Object.keys(errors)[0];
  if (first) setFocus(first);
}, [errors, setFocus]);
```

---

## Colour is not enough

A red border alone excludes colour-blind users. Always pair it with text, and ideally an icon.

---

## Server validation is mandatory

Client validation is a convenience for honest users. Anyone can send a request with `curl`. Run the same schema server-side:

```js
const result = schema.safeParse(await request.json());
if (!result.success) return Response.json({ errors: result.error.flatten() }, { status: 400 });
```

Sharing one schema between client and server is the strongest argument for Zod in a React stack.

## Reading the file

```jsx
function Upload() {
  const [file, setFile] = useState(null);

  function handleChange(e) {
    const selected = e.target.files?.[0];
    if (!selected) return;

    if (selected.size > 5 * 1024 * 1024) return setError('Max 5MB');
    if (!['image/png', 'image/jpeg'].includes(selected.type)) return setError('PNG or JPEG only');

    setFile(selected);
  }

  return <input type="file" accept="image/png,image/jpeg" onChange={handleChange} />;
}
```

A file input **cannot be controlled** — setting `value` on it is blocked by browsers for security. You always read from the event or a ref.

