## Security

Client-side type checking reads the filename extension and the browser-reported MIME type — both trivially spoofed. The server must verify the actual file contents, cap the size, store outside the web root, and never execute what was uploaded. Say this explicitly; it is often what the question is really probing.

For large files, upload directly to object storage with a pre-signed URL so the payload never passes through your API server.
